</span></span><span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:238.5pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{j\in\{\text{All Mask indices}\}}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{j}}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>All Mask indices</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{j\in\{\text{All Mask indices}\}}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{j}}})}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:127.2pt;height:30.8pt;vertical-align:-17.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(85.6pt,-6.6pt) scale(1.7559908236695,1.7559908236695) ;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{j\in\{\text{Top-K Mask indices}\}}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{j}}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>Top-K Mask indices</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{j\in\{\text{Top-K Mask indices}\}}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})]_{a^{j}}})}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Model initialization</span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="S3.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_bb ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_2" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:238.5pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Model Pretrained with Cross-Entropy Loss w.r.t. <math id="S3.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:127.2pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.1.1.1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Random Initialization</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></p>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Realizations of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{UPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{UPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> via the choice of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
We consider three reference policies—<math id="S3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{conf}}^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{conf}}^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}</annotation></semantics></math>—and summarize their associated divergence terms in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. In Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we provide the tractable surrogate <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> that is justified by Propositions <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ C.3 Surrogate loss of output-level KL divergence ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmprop3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ C.3 Surrogate loss of output-level KL divergence ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Surrogate loss of output-level KL divergence ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>. Since we are sampling the trajectory from old policy model while training, we design the estimator <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> that can be measured by the probability of the trajectories, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g_{\rm{ref}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\rm{ref}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For softmax realization, since <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns nonzero probability to all trajectories,
we can replace <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the tractable surrogate <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We parameterize <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> as the softmax distribution over all masked positions by default (see Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.2 Reformulating the problem as reinforcement learning ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>)) for softmax realization. For pretraining, although one could initialize by matching <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> via KL minimization, we observe stronger performance with cross-entropy. For <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists some sampled trajectory where <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g_{\rm{Top-K}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\rm{Top-K}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{Top\text{-}K}}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns zero probability to mask index out of Top-<math id="S3.SS4.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. In this regard, we reparameterize <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the softmax distribution of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> over the Top-<math id="S3.SS4.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> set only. This reparametrization gives two benefits: 1) we can utilize <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\rm{Top-K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\rm{Top-K}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero for all trajectory sampled from <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and 2) we do not need to pretrain policy model since it is same as <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{Top-K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{Top-K}}</annotation></semantics></math> when randomly initialized. In contrast, the determinism of <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math> renders <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> ill-posed whenever <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns zero mass to the chosen index, so we train with <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m31" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{CE}(g_{\mathrm{conf}}\!\parallel g_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CE</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CE}(g_{\mathrm{conf}}\!\parallel g_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> while retaining the regularized-MDP perspective. Full derivations and detailed explanations are provided in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Full Derivations for ℒ_UPO Realizations ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental results</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setting</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models and benchmarks.</span>
We evaluate on the widely used large-scale MDM <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaDA-8B-Instruct</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and four datasets: (i) logic-puzzle benchmarks—<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Sudoku</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Zebra</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shah et al., 2024</a>)</cite>—and (ii) mathematical-reasoning benchmarks—<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GSM8K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Math500</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lightman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generation protocols and rewards.</span>
We utilize <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaDA-8B-Instruct</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025</a>)</cite> for all experiments. For logic puzzles, the model receives a prompt and a masked solution; it then denoises by unmasking one position at a time. The reward is the fraction of slots predicted correctly (e.g., in <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Sudoku</span>, the proportion of blank cells filled with the correct digits). For mathematical reasoning, the model is given a problem and denoises a length-128 masked sequence. Following the <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaDA</span> generation protocol, we partition the 128 positions into four bins of size 32 and perform any-order sampling sequentially over the bins. The reward is <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the final answer matches the ground truth and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Training dynamics across reference policies</h3>

<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05725v1/sudoku_gsm8k.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/141;" width="548" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Training accuracy on <span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Sudoku</span> and <span id="S4.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GSM8K</span> under <math id="S4.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},D)</annotation></semantics></math> for different choices of <math id="S4.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math>. Reference realizations are summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. “Random initialization” denotes training a randomly initialized model with <math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},\varnothing,\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},\varnothing,\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train our policy model on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GSM8K</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Sudoku</span> by optimizing <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},D)</annotation></semantics></math> with three reference realizations from Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>: <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm conf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm conf}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm conf}^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm conf}^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm Top\text{-}K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm Top\text{-}K}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also report ablation that drops the divergence term, <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span> <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},\varnothing,\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}(g_{\phi},\varnothing,\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>, with a randomly initialized policy, which is conceptually equivalent to <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DColT</span>. The result is shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Training dynamics across reference policies ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
The strongest configuration depends on the task: on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Sudoku</span>, max-confidence realization achieves the best accuracy, while on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GSM8K</span>, Top-<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> realization performs best. We conjecture that in <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GSM8K</span>, restricting exploration to the Top–<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> indices stabilizes learning under <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}</annotation></semantics></math> due to the much larger number of masked tokens.
Across the two benchmarks, our optimal configuration outperforms the randomly initialized model—that is, <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DColT</span> (green line)—by margins of at least 2% and 3%, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
