<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related works</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discrete Diffusion Models.</span> Diffusion probabilistic models have become the state-of-the-art approach for continuous data domains such as images, audio, and video, by iteratively denoising Gaussian-corrupted inputs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Extending this success to <em id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">discrete</em> data (e.g. text or sequences) has led to the development of discrete diffusion models built on discrete-state Markov chains rather than continuous noise processes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoogeboom et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. (2024)</a></cite> proposed SEDD, which utilizes theoretical score entropy objective.
Meanwhile, masked diffusion models (MDMs), which utilize an absorbing mask strategy, have emerged as a leading class of discrete diffusion models for text generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. By using an absorbing masking state, MDMs simplify the corruption process: once a token is masked, it remains masked until generation, analogous to absorbing diffusion in continuous models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. This simplification yields a clean and principled training recipe aligned with continuous-time diffusion theory, including an evidence lower bound (ELBO) objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Beyond continuous-time discrete diffusion, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al. (2025)</a></cite> provides a time-agnostic training framework and simple cross-entropy loss. These advances have significantly closed the performance gap between MDMs and traditional autoregressive models on language tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025</a>)</cite> when the scale of the model is similar.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unmasking Strategy in Masked Diffusion Inference.</span> A crucial factor for MDM performance is the <em id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unmasking strategy</em> used during inference—i.e., how the model decides which masked tokens to reveal at each generation step. While MDMs have shown superior performance on text generations, earlier works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ou et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shih et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2021</a>)</cite> have empirically observed that a random unmasking strategy is suboptimal. Moreover, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite> proves that no polynomial-time algorithm can solve any-order generation; <em id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="A1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span>, we cannot train MDMs that exactly recovers the real data distribution for all masked sentences. However, they empirically show that selecting unmasking tokens via max-confidence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang et al., 2022</a>)</cite> or max-margin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025</a>)</cite> at inference time can bypass sub-hard instances and even outperform ARMs. As a result, contemporary large-scale MDMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025</a>)</cite> commonly adopt max-confidence scheduling at inference.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05725v1/x1.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/149;" width="548" height="149"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>The structure of our unmasking policy model. The model is composed of a single Transformer layer and a 3-layer MLP. In inference time, the model proceeds as follows: 1) Given an input sentence, we run the base MDMs transformer and extract a feature. 2) This feature branches into two paths: first, the base MDMs continue to produce a prediction of token distribution, and second, fed to the policy model’s transformer layer. 3) We concatenate the extracted feature with the base MDM’s Top-K probabilities. 4) The concatenated feature is then processed by a 3-layer MLP to yield a policy over unmasking positions.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training recipe in detail</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we explain our memory-efficient training recipe in detail. We provide full derivations of various reference policy realizations (Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Full Derivations for ℒ_UPO Realizations ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), and algorithms for training and generating (Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Algorithms ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>). For a deeper understanding of our memory-efficient training algorithm and model architecture, we first provide notations and model inference in detail.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Policy model inference process.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our rationale behind policy model structure is two: 1) utilizing the MDM’s knowledge (extracted feature), which allows for avoiding from-scratch training and allow memory-efficient training, and 2) utilizing the MDM’s token prediction distribution, which can help the model mimic the behavior of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The main paper outlined the policy model’s inference at a high level; here, we provide a notation and description of how, given a masked sentence <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model generates an unmasking trajectory. For reference, we reproduce the model architecture from the main paper (Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) as Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix A Related works ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. To recap, the unmasking policy model is parameterized as a softmax over masked positions using a learnable scorer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\phi}({\bm{x}})\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\phi}(a^{i}\,|\,{\bm{x}}_{n})=\frac{\exp\!\big([h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}\big)}{\sum_{i^{\prime}=1}^{n}\exp\!\big([h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i^{\prime}}}\big)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\phi}(a^{i}\,|\,{\bm{x}}_{n})=\frac{\exp\!\big([h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}\big)}{\sum_{i^{\prime}=1}^{n}\exp\!\big([h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i^{\prime}}}\big)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th mask of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As illustrated in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix A Related works ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the policy model decomposes as
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=(\phi_{\rm MLP},\phi_{\rm TF})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=(\phi_{\rm MLP},\phi_{\rm TF})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\rm TF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\rm TF}</annotation></semantics></math> is a 1-layer Transformer
and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\rm MLP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\rm MLP}</annotation></semantics></math> is a 3-layer MLP. We similarly write the MDM as
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=(\theta_{\rm TF},\theta_{\rm MLP})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=(\theta_{\rm TF},\theta_{\rm MLP})</annotation></semantics></math> with a feature extractor transformer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\rm TF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\rm TF}</annotation></semantics></math> and a token prediction head
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\rm MLP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\rm MLP}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the current masked sequence <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and selected mask <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the MDM computes the token distribution as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{n}=\theta_{\rm TF}({\bm{x}}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{a^{i}}=\mathbf{H}_{n}[a^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{n}=\theta_{\rm TF}({\bm{x}}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{a^{i}}=\mathbf{H}_{n}[a^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}}=\theta_{\rm MLP}(\mathbf{u}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|},\qquad\pi_{\theta}\!\left(x^{a^{i}}_{n-1}=c\,\middle|\,{\bm{x}}_{n}\right)=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}})_{c}\;\;\;\;(c\in\mathcal{V})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}}=\theta_{\rm MLP}(\mathbf{u}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{V}|},\qquad\pi_{\theta}\!\left(x^{a^{i}}_{n-1}=c\,\middle|\,{\bm{x}}_{n}\right)=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}})_{c}\;\;\;\;(c\in\mathcal{V}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the output dimension of the transformer feature. Let
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}}=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}}=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{z}_{a^{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> the token posterior at index <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with dimension <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
The policy encoder first refines the sequence features,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}_{n}=\phi_{\rm TF}(\mathbf{H}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{u}}_{a^{i}}=\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}_{n}[a^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}_{n}=\phi_{\rm TF}(\mathbf{H}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{u}}_{a^{i}}=\widetilde{\mathbf{H}}_{n}[a^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the vector of the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> largest probabilities of
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, sorted in descending order. We form the concatenated feature</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{s}_{a^{i}}=\big[\,\widetilde{\mathbf{u}}_{a^{i}}\;;\;\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}})\,\big]\in\mathbb{R}^{d+K}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><mi>TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{s}_{a^{i}}=\big[\,\widetilde{\mathbf{u}}_{a^{i}}\;;\;\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{p}_{a^{i}})\,\big]\in\mathbb{R}^{d+K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and map it to a scalar score via the 3-layer MLP:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}=\phi_{\rm MLP}(\mathbf{s}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}=\phi_{\rm MLP}(\mathbf{s}_{a^{i}})\in\mathbb{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Finally, the unmasking policy over the masked index set is the softmax
of these scores (Eq. (<a href="#A2.E21" title="In Policy model inference process. ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Full Derivations for <math id="A2.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm UPO}</annotation></semantics></math> Realizations</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General formulations.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To recap, our final objective is given as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm{UPO}}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm{ref}},D)=\mathbb{E}_{{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{Q}},\{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}^{(g)},a_{1:L}^{(g)}\}_{g=1}^{G}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}}\Biggl[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{g}^{G}\Biggl(\Bigl(\frac{1}{L}\sum_{n=1}^{L}\min\bigl(\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}A_{g}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm{UPO}}(g_{\phi},g_{\rm{ref}},D)=\mathbb{E}_{{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{Q}},\{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}^{(g)},a_{1:L}^{(g)}\}_{g=1}^{G}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}}\Biggl[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{g}^{G}\Biggl(\Bigl(\frac{1}{L}\sum_{n=1}^{L}\min\bigl(\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}A_{g},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{clip}(\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)A_{g}\bigr)\Bigr)-\beta\cdot D(p_{g_{\phi}}||p_{g_{\rm{ref}}})\Biggr)\Biggr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{clip}(\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)A_{g}\bigr)\Bigr)-\beta\cdot D(p_{g_{\phi}}||p_{g_{\rm{ref}}})\Biggr)\Biggr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The divergence term <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E23" title="In General formulations. ‣ B.1 Full Derivations for ℒ_UPO Realizations ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) is a <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">functional</em> that, given a prompt
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a full trajectory <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau=({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L})</annotation></semantics></math>, and models
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, returns a scalar estimate. Formally,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},\pi_{\theta}}:\;\mathcal{Q}\times\mathcal{X}_{0:L}\times\mathcal{A}_{1:L}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref},\pi_{\theta}}:\;\mathcal{Q}\times\mathcal{X}_{0:L}\times\mathcal{A}_{1:L}\rightarrow\mathbb{R},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and its empirical expectation serves as a tractable estimator of the <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">output-level</span> KL divergence <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\rm KL}\!\big(p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\,\|\,p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\rm KL}\!\big(p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\,\|\,p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. Following Proposition <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ C.3 Surrogate loss of output-level KL divergence ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmprop3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ C.3 Surrogate loss of output-level KL divergence ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we can decrease the <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">output-level</span> KL divergence with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L},{\mathbf{q}})={\rm StopGrad}\!\Bigl(\tfrac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}\cdot\bigl(1+\log\tfrac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr)\Bigr)\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:4.164em;" width="4.164em"><mi>StopGrad</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L},{\mathbf{q}})={\rm StopGrad}\!\Bigl(\tfrac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}\cdot\bigl(1+\log\tfrac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr)\Bigr)\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi},g_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity. We can convert <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}|{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{n=1}^{L}g(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})\cdot\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}|{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n},{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{n=1}^{L}g(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})\cdot\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}|{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n},{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E24" title="In General formulations. ‣ B.1 Full Derivations for ℒ_UPO Realizations ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}(\cdot)={\rm StopGrad}\!\Bigl(\prod_{n=1}^{L}\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}\cdot\bigl(1+\sum\log\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}{g_{{\rm{ref}}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}\bigr)\Bigr)\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.164em;" width="4.164em"><mi>StopGrad</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}(\cdot)={\rm StopGrad}\!\Bigl(\prod_{n=1}^{L}\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}\cdot\bigl(1+\sum\log\frac{g_{\phi}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}{g_{{\rm{ref}}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})}\bigr)\Bigr)\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We already computed <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> while sampling, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> while computing reward-maximization objective term in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{UPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>UPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{UPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not require network evaluations. Therefore, we can measure <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> without no additional computation. Furthermore, since <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is summation, we can perform gradient update token-by-token, which allows tractable and memory-efficient training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Softmax realization.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For softmax realization of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> given as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\exp({\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a^{i}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n})/\tau})}{\sum_{a^{j}}\sum_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\exp({\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n})/\tau})},\;\;\text{s.t.}\;\lim_{\tau\rightarrow 0+}g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}=g_{\text{conf}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>conf</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\exp({\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a^{i}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n})/\tau})}{\sum_{a^{j}}\sum_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\exp({\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n})/\tau})},\;\;\text{s.t.}\;\lim_{\tau\rightarrow 0+}g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}=g_{\text{conf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, since <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns non-zero probability to every unmasking index, we can estimate the terminal KL divergence with a sampled trajectory. We utilize <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In General formulations. ‣ B.1 Full Derivations for ℒ_UPO Realizations ‣ Appendix B Training recipe in detail ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>)) by replacing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Top-<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> realization</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Top-<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> realization of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>conf</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> given as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\rm{Top-K}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\rm{Top-K}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\cdot\textbf{1}(a^{i}\in\underset{{a^{j}}}{\rm{argtopk}}(\max_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n}))),\;\;\text{s.t.}\;g_{\rm{Top-1}}=g_{\rm{conf}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">1</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>argtopk</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">j</mi></msup></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\cdot\textbf{1}(a^{i}\in\underset{{a^{j}}}{\rm{argtopk}}(\max_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n}))),\;\;\text{s.t.}\;g_{\rm{Top-1}}=g_{\rm{conf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we reparametrize <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})=\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{a^{j}\in{\rm{argtopk}}\max\pi_{\theta}(\cdot)}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{j}}})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>argtopk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})=\frac{\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{i}}})}{\sum_{a^{j}\in{\rm{argtopk}}\max\pi_{\theta}(\cdot)}\exp({[h_{\phi}({\bm{x}}_{n})]_{a^{j}}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is the softmax distribution of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> on the Top-<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> set of unmasking positions. This reparametrization offers two advantages: 1) when <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is randomly initialized, we can expect <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}=g_{\rm{Top-K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}=g_{\rm{Top-K}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and 2) for sampled trajectory, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{Top-K}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{Top-K}}(a_{n}|{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero for all <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[1,L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[1,L]</annotation></semantics></math> since we sample from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can train <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{Top-K}}}</annotation></semantics></math> from scratch with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}=g_{\rm{Top-K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}=g_{\rm{Top-K}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Max-confidence realization.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For max-confidence realization of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math> given as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\text{conf}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})=\textbf{1}\bigl(a^{i}=\argmax_{a^{j}}(\max_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n}))\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>conf</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">1</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\text{conf}}(a^{i}|{\bm{x}}_{n})=\textbf{1}\bigl(a^{i}=\argmax_{a^{j}}(\max_{c\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{n-1}^{a^{j}}=c|{\bm{x}}_{n}))\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic. The terminal KL divergence <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\rm KL}\!\big(p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\,\|\,p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\rm KL}\!\big(p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\,\|\,p_{g_{\rm ref}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is stochastic, but we cannot empirically estimate the terminal KL divergence with sampled trajectory since there exists trajectory sampled from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math> is 0 for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\rm{conf}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\rm{conf}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we just utilize cross-entropy given as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm{CE}}_{g_{\phi},g_{\rm{conf}},\pi_{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L},{\mathbf{q}})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{{\bm{x}}_{n}}}g_{\rm{conf}}(a|{\bm{x}}_{n})\log g_{\theta}(a|{\bm{x}}_{n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>CE</mi><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm{CE}}_{g_{\phi},g_{\rm{conf}},\pi_{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L},{\mathbf{q}})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{{\bm{x}}_{n}}}g_{\rm{conf}}(a|{\bm{x}}_{n})\log g_{\theta}(a|{\bm{x}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Although not theoretical, we can expect to regularize <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> being far away from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have empirically confirmed the performance gain (Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Algorithms</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Generalized Sampling of MDMs</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Sequence length <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, vocabulary <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, pretrained masked diffusion model <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, unmasking policy <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{L}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{L}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow L\ \textbf{to}\ 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">to</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow L\ \textbf{to}\ 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              sample <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}\sim g(a|{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}\sim g(a|{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> unmasking token distribution. <span id="alg1.l4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(\{a^{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(\{a^{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              sample <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n-1}^{a_{n}}\sim\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a_{n}}|{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n-1}^{a_{n}}\sim\pi_{\theta}(x_{n-1}^{a_{n}}|{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> per-position categorical probabilities
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n-1}\leftarrow\{x_{n}^{1},x_{n}^{2},\dots,x_{n}^{a_{n}-1},x_{n-1}^{a_{n}},x_{n}^{a_{n}+1},\dots,x^{L}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n-1}\leftarrow\{x_{n}^{1},x_{n}^{2},\dots,x_{n}^{a_{n}-1},x_{n-1}^{a_{n}},x_{n}^{a_{n}+1},\dots,x^{L}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Memory-efficient training of the unmasking policy model</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Pretrained masked diffusion model <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> composed of feature extracting transformer <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\rm{TF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\rm{TF}}</annotation></semantics></math> and token estimator <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\rm{MLP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\rm{MLP}}</annotation></semantics></math>, unmasking policy model <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> composed of 1-layer transformer <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\rm{TF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\rm{TF}}</annotation></semantics></math> and 3-Layer MLP <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\rm{MLP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\rm{MLP}}</annotation></semantics></math>, divergence loss <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, reference policy <math id="alg2.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\rm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\rm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, prompt distribution <math id="alg2.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of inner updates <math id="alg2.l1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not converge <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sampling phase</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">with</span> <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch.no_grad()</span>:

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}\leftarrow g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}\leftarrow g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
               Sample a prompt <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{q}}\sim\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{q}}\sim\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
               Sample G trajectories <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}^{(g)},a_{1:L}^{(g)}\}_{g=1}^{G}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}^{(g)},a_{1:L}^{(g)}\}_{g=1}^{G}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{q}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in[G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in[G]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> while sampling, save <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{H}}_{n}^{(g)}=\theta_{\rm{TF}}({\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{H}}_{n}^{(g)}=\theta_{\rm{TF}}({\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi_{old}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi_{old}}(a_{n}^{(g)}|{\bm{x}}_{n}^{(g)})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
