<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{supp}(p_{\theta^{*}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}}))\subseteq\operatorname{supp}(p_{g_{\mathrm{ref}}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}(p_{\theta^{*}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}}))\subseteq\operatorname{supp}(p_{g_{\mathrm{ref}}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the inequality in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Theorem 2 (Reference-KL Tightening for MDM Policy Improvement). ‣ 3.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) holds. Accordingly, inequality in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="In Theorem 2 (Reference-KL Tightening for MDM Policy Improvement). ‣ 3.3 Theoretical analysis ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) holds where <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta^{*}}=p_{\rm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{*}}=p_{\rm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> for ideal MDM <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Surrogate loss of output-level reward maximization</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal here is to show that the output-level reward maximization term in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.2 Reformulating the problem as reinforcement learning ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) can be converted into a tractable token-wise reward maximization term. The conclusion of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Output–Token Level Gradient Alignment (informal)). ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> aligns with conventional RL that have developed with rigorous proofs, yet in our setting, where training the MDM unmasking policy, the assumptions are slightly different.
More specifically, our MDP is a finite-horizon MDP with fixed length <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (text length is determined), sparse reward (only a verifiable reward for the terminal state exists), and non-stationary (for different time steps, states do not overlap).
To fill this gap, we rigorously show that Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Output–Token Level Gradient Alignment (informal)). ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We cannot even directly apply the policy gradient theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton et al., 1999</a>)</cite>, which is essential in the proof.
Therefore, we start with justifying how the policy gradient theorem also works in our framework, which can be easily proven:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Policy gradient theorem in sparse-reward, finite-horizon, episodic, and non-stationary MDP)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a horizon <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> let the state space be <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume the spaces are pairwise disjoint: <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{n}\cap\mathcal{X}_{j}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{n}\cap\mathcal{X}_{j}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>.
At step <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>, from state <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> a discrete action <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn from a stochastic policy <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the environment transitions to the next layer’s state
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{n-1}\in\mathcal{X}_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{n-1}\in\mathcal{X}_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> according to dynamics <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{x}}_{n-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{x}}_{n-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume the start state is fixed as <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The trajectory is <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau=({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=({\bm{x}}_{0:L},a_{1:L})</annotation></semantics></math> with joint density</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\prod_{n=1}^{L}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\,\pi({\bm{x}}_{n-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\prod_{n=1}^{L}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\,\pi({\bm{x}}_{n-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rewards are <em id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">terminal-only</em>: <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
The objective is the expected terminal reward</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\phi)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\phi)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the value function and state-action value function under <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}\right],\qquad Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}\right],\qquad Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the above assumptions, the policy gradient depends only on the policy <math id="Thmlemma2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\nabla_{\phi}V_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{{\bm{x}}\in\mathcal{X}_{1}\cup\mathcal{X}_{2}\dots\cup\mathcal{X}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}})\sum_{a}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}},a)\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a|{\bm{x}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\nabla_{\phi}V_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{{\bm{x}}\in\mathcal{X}_{1}\cup\mathcal{X}_{2}\dots\cup\mathcal{X}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}})\sum_{a}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}},a)\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a|{\bm{x}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\phi)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}[r({\bm{x}}_{0})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\phi)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}[r({\bm{x}}_{0})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the log-derivative trick,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,\nabla_{\phi}p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,\nabla_{\phi}p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})\,\nabla_{\phi}\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\tau}r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})\,\nabla_{\phi}\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since only the policy <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})+\text{const}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})+\text{const},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\log p_{g_{\phi}}(\tau\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})=\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Taking conditional expectations with respect to <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> yields
for each <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\!\Big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\!\Big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\,\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}}\!\Big[\mathbb{E}\!\big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}\big]\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}}\!\Big[\mathbb{E}\!\big[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\mid{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}\big]\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(tower property)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}}\!\Big[Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n}}\!\Big[Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\;Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\;Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})=p({\bm{x}}_{n})g(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})=p({\bm{x}}_{n})g(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{n}\in\mathcal{X}_{n}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\sum_{a_{n}\in\mathcal{A}_{n}}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})\;\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g\,\nabla\log g=\nabla g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\,\nabla\log g=\nabla g</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})=\Pr_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}(X_{n}={\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})=\Pr_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}(X_{n}={\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})=p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\,g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n},a_{n})=p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{n})\,g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> are the marginals induced by the rollout distribution. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}J(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}}_{L})}\!\left[r({\bm{x}}_{0})\sum_{n=1}^{L}\nabla_{\phi}\log g_{\phi}(a_{n}\mid{\bm{x}}_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}\in\mathcal{X}_{1}\cup\mathcal{X}_{2}\dots\cup\mathcal{X}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}})\sum_{a}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}},a)\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a|{\bm{x}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{x}}\in\mathcal{X}_{1}\cup\mathcal{X}_{2}\dots\cup\mathcal{X}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}})\sum_{a}Q_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}},a)\nabla_{\phi}g_{\phi}(a|{\bm{x}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">which ends the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This can also be proved in another way, just iteratively deriving the <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}V_{g_{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}V_{g_{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Policy gradient theorem in sparse-reward, finite-horizon, episodic, and non-stationary MDP). ‣ C.2 Surrogate loss of output-level reward maximization ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we can prove our main objective as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Output–Token Level Gradient Alignment (informal)). ‣ 3.4 Practical realization of unmasking policy optimization ‣ 3 Improving Unmasking Policy Beyond a Reference Policy ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We derive <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{token}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>token</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{token}}</annotation></semantics></math> separately. Then, by applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Policy gradient theorem in sparse-reward, finite-horizon, episodic, and non-stationary MDP). ‣ C.2 Surrogate loss of output-level reward maximization ‣ Appendix C Detailed Proof ‣ Improving Discrete Diffusion Unmasking Policies Beyond Explicit Reference Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> to <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a form that matches <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{token}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>token</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{token}}</annotation></semantics></math>. First, expanding <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that it is equivalent to maximizing the advantage from the initial state:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[\frac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim p_{g_{\phi_{\rm{old}}}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[\frac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\frac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})\frac{p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}{p_{g_{\phi_{\rm old}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})}A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{X}}\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we derive <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>output</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\rm{output}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\phi}\biggr[\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]\biggl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">[</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\phi}\biggr[\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0:L}\sim p_{g_{\phi}}(\cdot\mid{\mathbf{q}})}\bigr[A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]\biggl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\phi}\biggr[\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]\biggl]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">[</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\phi}\biggr[\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{q}}\sim\rho_{\mathcal{Q}}}\bigr[\sum_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{x}}_{1},...{\bm{x}}_{L}}p_{g_{\phi}}({\bm{x}}_{0:L}\mid{\mathbf{q}})A({\mathbf{q}},{\bm{x}}_{0})\bigl]\biggl]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
